2026-11-25T09:09:31.7361826Z   ok   a budget refusal names a tail-cut site as one that survived every shared driver, a never-started one as not started, and a tail-cut-only run as no verdict measured -- all refused, none PASSED
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7362088Z   ok   mutation-nightly, mutation-ledger and the pin step each pass a budget
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7362523Z   ok   a budget cut falls on an anchor boundary, so no anchor is split and no killed twin is listed for a human verdict
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7362849Z   ok   a mutant whose driver timed out runs no further driver
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7363194Z   ok   a twin granted with its anchor is started even after a dearer site between them closes the pool
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7363380Z   ok   the drain lists no site of an anchor the budget split
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7363585Z   ok   a timed-out mutant releases the EXCLUSIVE run it reserved
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7364023Z   ok   a run whose mutants all timed out or went unstarted is refused by cause, and a partial PASSED counts the timed-out ones
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7364539Z   ok   the pin drive holds four (mutant, driver) runs in flight at once -- the split exists, and is not drive_pool's one-mutant-at-a-time schedule
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7364911Z   ok   the split's verdicts and pins are byte-identical to the serial schedule's, the named killer included
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7365358Z   ok   under the split a timed-out driver is never a kill: the mutant runs nothing further, reads SKIP-TIMED-OUT, and pins nothing
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7365833Z   ok   the split's budget admission divides the outstanding work by the workers, measuring a pool the serial estimate closes after two
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7366269Z   ok   budget admission charges no pair reach_skip frees, in both schedules, and main() hands the schedule its reach predicate
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7366775Z   ok   the split admits a mutant on its shared work and charges the EXCLUSIVE tail only to a survivor that reaches it; a lazy driver costs one run
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7367300Z   ok   the pin shards are disjoint, cover the pool and keep an anchor's twins together; their merge is measured when any shard measured, one shard too
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7367859Z   ok   a shard whose files hold no whole-line comment inherits the whole pool's null control: null_for reads the pre-split pool, and main() wires it that way
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7368454Z   ok   CI-17: every job pip-installing the hash-locked requirements caches pip on their lock files, and a job stripped of its cache lines is refused (null control)
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7368983Z   ok   the pin shard count scales with the diff's new sites, five a shard, capped at twelve, and sizes the matrix the shards run, four at a time (CI-7)
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7369353Z   ok   and a plan step without always(), or a pin job still reading the old plan job, is refused (null control)
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7369890Z   ok   the pin summary counts budget cuts, exclusive-tail cuts and timeouts apart from survivors, and names a survivor's remedy only when one survived
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7370275Z   ok   main() routes the pin-measurement phase through the split and every other mode through drive_pool
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7370770Z   ok   a site holding a survivor_triage mark is recognised as triaged; a moved line, an unmarked site and an empty triage are not (R9-F10.13)
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7371323Z   ok   the nightly reports a pin its script did not kill, and never reads a site the budget, a timeout or another driver left unrun as re-verified (R9-F10.13)
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7371997Z   ok   a triage-marked site is driven by every driver but the one that judges the marks, and left out when that is its only driver; an unmarked site keeps it (R9-F10.13)
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7372434Z   ok   a pinned site's killer is driven first however dear it is; an unpinned site and a stale pin keep the cost order (R9-F10.13)
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7373244Z   ok   --anchor re-drives one site: the real pin is reproduced, a pin planted on a script that does not kill it is reported NOT REPRODUCED after its own run, and nothing is recorded (R9-F10.13)
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7374097Z   ok   a re-driven pin is not reproduced by a driver that only sees the row the mutant made stale: the row is hidden from the mutant's tree, and a code check still kills it (R10 mutation-anchor)
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7374563Z   ok   --anchor still reproduces the real pin when the anchored file already carries the mutation lane's comment-only null control
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7375236Z   ok   invalidated_rows names exactly the rows pinned to a rewritten line, the ledger without them agrees with the rewritten file, and an unpinned line names none (R10 mutation-anchor)
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7375517Z   ok   mutation-nightly rotates its seed by date and surfaces the report (R9-F10.13)
2026-11-25T09:09:31.7375756Z   ok   a changed-scope pool draws only sites on lines the diff modified
